---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const rolloutCode = `from google.adk.evaluation import AgentEvaluator
from google.adk.runners import Runner
from google.adk.sessions import InMemorySessionService

session_service = InMemorySessionService()
runner = Runner(
    agent=root_agent_v2,
    app_name="maintenance_agent",
    session_service=session_service,
)

evaluator = AgentEvaluator(
    agent=root_agent_v2,
    eval_set_id="maintenance_canary_v2_2026_05",
)

# Gate canary rollout on eval + shadow traces first.
eval_result = await evaluator.evaluate(input_text="Diagnose alarm E118 on M-42")

async for event in runner.run_async(
    user_id="shadow-user",
    session_id="shadow-session",
    new_message=user_message,
):
    if event.is_final_response():
        log_shadow_outcome(event)`;
---

<SiteLayout current="rollout-lifecycle" title="Rollout lifecycle">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Optional 06C</p>
      <h1>Rollout lifecycle: canary, versioning, and rollback.</h1>
      <p>
        Production agent changes should ship through a controlled lifecycle:
        evaluate, shadow, canary, expand, and rollback fast when signals degrade.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mini-diagram react-diagram harness-diagram" aria-label="Rollout stages" style="margin-bottom: 48px; margin-left: -40px; margin-right: -40px; border-radius: 20px;">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1080 300" role="img">
        <defs>
          <marker id="react-arrow" markerHeight="8" markerWidth="8" orient="auto" refX="7" refY="4">
            <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 Z" fill="var(--accent)"></path>
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <g class="react-links" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="8 8" style="animation: data-flow 1.5s linear infinite; opacity: 0.8;">
          <path d="M 240 150 H 320" marker-end="url(#react-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 480 150 H 560" marker-end="url(#react-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 720 150 H 800" marker-end="url(#react-arrow)"></path>
        </g>
        <style>
          .rollout-text { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; fill: var(--ink); font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; }
          .rollout-sub { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; fill: var(--muted); font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace; }
        </style>
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="80" y="100" width="160" height="100" rx="16"></rect>
          <text x="160" y="142" class="rollout-text" text-anchor="middle">Shadow</text>
          <text x="160" y="168" class="rollout-sub" text-anchor="middle">0% impact</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg is-planner">
          <rect x="320" y="100" width="160" height="100" rx="50"></rect>
          <text x="400" y="142" class="rollout-text" text-anchor="middle">Canary</text>
          <text x="400" y="168" class="rollout-sub" text-anchor="middle">1% traffic</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg is-critic">
          <rect x="560" y="100" width="160" height="100" rx="50"></rect>
          <text x="640" y="142" class="rollout-text" text-anchor="middle">Ramp</text>
          <text x="640" y="168" class="rollout-sub" text-anchor="middle">10-50%</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg is-done">
          <rect x="800" y="100" width="160" height="100" rx="16"></rect>
          <text x="880" y="142" class="rollout-text" text-anchor="middle">GA</text>
          <text x="880" y="168" class="rollout-sub" text-anchor="middle">100% prod</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="signal-panel signal-panel--definitions" style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <div>
        <article>
          <span>Strategy</span>
          <strong>Canary first</strong>
          <p>Expose new behavior to a small traffic slice before broad rollout.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Traceability</span>
          <strong>Versioned runtime</strong>
          <p>Map each agent version to a specific eval set and release decision.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Safety</span>
          <strong>Fast rollback</strong>
          <p>Keep rollback paths mechanical: route traffic back to last known-good immediately.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Release sequence</p>
      <h2>Use staged exposure, not big-bang deploys.</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="timeline-list">
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Pre-release eval gate</strong>
          <p>Run regression evals for tool choice, trajectory quality, and grounding before traffic moves.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Shadow run</strong>
          <p>Replay production-like inputs to the new version and log traces without side effects.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Canary slice</strong>
          <p>Shift a small percentage of live traffic and monitor p95 latency, cost/task, and failure classes.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">04</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Progressive ramp</strong>
          <p>Increase exposure only when quality and reliability stay above threshold for a fixed window.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">05</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Rollback trigger</strong>
          <p>If safety or quality SLOs regress, switch routing to previous version first, investigate second.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <figure class="code-card code-card--standalone">
      <figcaption>
        <span class="lang-pill">python</span>
        <span class="code-filename">adk_rollout_gate.py</span>
        <span class="code-tag">AgentEvaluator + run_async shadow check</span>
      </figcaption>
      <Code code={rolloutCode} lang="python" theme="github-light" />
    </figure>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Operational checklist</p>
      <h2>What must be true before each release stage.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="signal-panel signal-panel--definitions" style="margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <div>
        <article>
          <span>Pre-flight</span>
          <strong>Canary readiness</strong>
          <p>Eval pass-rate at or above baseline, no new critical failure mode classes, and stable tool-call safety checks.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Metadata</span>
          <strong>Version discipline</strong>
          <p>Each deployment references a versioned prompt/instruction set, model config, and eval snapshot ID.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Operations</span>
          <strong>Rollback readiness</strong>
          <p>On-call runbook, one-click routing rollback, and replay path using saved sessions/traces are all tested.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mechanism-note">
      A rollback is not failure; it is a reliability feature. Teams that ship
      agents safely optimize for short mean-time-to-revert, not perfect first deploys.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
